==============================================================================
(a) vs (b) — WHAT MORE TRAINING DATA DID
==============================================================================

  Same test year, same features, same estimator, same seed, same
  metric. Only the training data differs: 39 fitted dates in one
  year, against ? fitted dates across three.

  stratified margin  (a) +0.1634   (b) +0.1418   change -0.0215
  model AUC          (a) 0.7281    (b) 0.7030    change -0.0251
  baseline AUC       (a) 0.5647    (b) 0.5611    change -0.0036

  The baseline is ensemble spread on identical rows, so it SHOULD be
  unchanged between (a) and (b) — it does not depend on training
  data at all. A non-zero change there is a bug, not a finding.
  -> IT MOVED. Investigate before reading anything else here.

